=== 2. DEMOTION (the step that was missing) ===

🚨 THE TRIGGER IS MECHANICAL. NO JUDGEMENT. (rewritten Aug 24, 2026)

  IF step 0 reports MORE THAN 2 BLOCKS in current_phase.md, demote AT LEAST ONE - the oldest -
  during THIS pass, and COMMIT AFTER EACH ONE. Never zero. Then continue with the rest.

  "At least one" is what makes the process DRAIN: every pass adds one handoff and removes one or more
  blocks, so the file is net-zero-or-better BY CONSTRUCTION rather than append-only by construction.

  ⚠️ THE SAFETY INVARIANT IS THE COMMIT BETWEEN BLOCKS, NOT A CAP ON THE COUNT. An earlier draft of
  this rule said "exactly one" to force the minimum, which would have been a mistake in the other
  direction: at one per pass a 39-block backlog needs ~37 passes, i.e. months, so the rule would
  stop the bleeding and never converge. Doing five blocks with a commit after each is NOT the
  batching that 2e forbids - batching is several deletions sharing one commit, where a mistake is
  unrecoverable because there is no intermediate state to go back to.

  📌 BACKLOG. Steady state is 2. Update this line every time you demote, so the next session can see
     whether this is actually converging rather than having to re-derive it.
