  If you want something to happen reliably, gate it on a number a script can print.

  Also still true: demote whenever a phase closes, whatever the block count says.

  a. Pick the block: the OLDEST in current_phase.md, or the largest closed/dormant-phase block in
     MEMORY.md's CURRENT STATE.
  b. ROUTE IT - three outcomes, not one. Read the block and sort its content:
       LIVE RULE  -> it still governs behaviour today. PROMOTE it to its proper home (MEMORY.md,
                     education/METHOD.md, education/CONVENTIONS.md), do NOT bury it in a phase file.
                     A rule filed as history is a rule that stops being followed.
       HISTORY    -> narrative, measurements, session log. COPY VERBATIM into the phase file.
       COVERED    -> the knowledge already lives somewhere appropriate. Delete, no copy needed.
     Most blocks are a mix, so expect to split one block across all three.

  ⚠️ ASK "IS THE KNOWLEDGE PRESERVED SOMEWHERE APPROPRIATE?", NOT "IS THIS TEXT DUPLICATED?"
     Those are different questions and they give opposite answers. Measured Aug 21-24, 2026 on the
     Phase 15 block: an exact-line comparison said 320 of 320 substantive lines were absent from
     phase15_education_program.md, which framed the demotion as high-risk archaeology. It was not.
     The block's load-bearing content - the "Andrew runs the commands" driver split, the one-command
     loop, the repetition rule - was ALREADY in education/METHOD.md, in its correct home, promoted
     there at the time. The text was not duplicated; the knowledge was safe.
     ⭐ A verbatim-text check answers a question about STORAGE. You need the answer about MEANING.

  🚨 AND VALIDATE THE TOOL BEFORE TRUSTING ITS NUMBER. The first version of that comparison reported
     "100% missing" for all four candidate blocks. It was broken, not alarming: it stripped markdown
     (* ` _ #) out of the search key but not out of the file being searched, so it was looking for
     text that could not exist. A POSITIVE CONTROL exposed it - searching a file for its OWN lines
     found only 7 of 25. ⛔ Any script you write to justify a deletion must first be shown to find
     something it should find. A coverage number from an unvalidated tool is worse than no number,
     because it licenses a delete.
  c. Replace the block in MEMORY.md with a PHASE INDEX row (see format below).
  d. VERIFY, from the shell, not from a read-back (this repo is on CIFS - see MEMORY.md gotcha):
       wc -l MEMORY.md
       git diff MEMORY.md | rg '^-' | rg -v '^---'     # read EVERY removed line
     Every deleted line must be one you meant to delete AND must now exist in the phase file.
  e. COMMIT before demoting the next block, so any loss is one `git show` away.

🚨 Silent loss of a hard-won finding is the worst failure mode this project has. One block at a
time, verified, committed between steps. Never batch demotions.

